Algorithm: 

Step 1: Assume the first day’s price as the minimum buying price.
Step 2: Initialize a variable to store maximum profit as 0.
Step 3: Traverse the price array starting from the second day.
Step 4: For each day:
        If the current price is lower than the stored buying price, update the buying price.
        Otherwise, calculate the profit by subtracting the buying price from the current price.
Step 5: If this profit is greater than the stored maximum profit, update the maximum profit.
Step 6: Continue this process until all days are checked.
Step 7: Return the maximum profit.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)


-----> Code <----

class Solution {
    public int maxProfit(int[] prices) {
        int buy=prices[0],pro=0;
        for(int i=1;i<prices.length;i++){
            if(prices[i]<buy){
                buy=prices[i];
            }else{
                int x=prices[i]-buy;
                if(pro<x){
                    pro=x;
                }
            }
        }
        return pro;
    }
}
